im to one  okay  she says i actually was rob when i was  living in harlem my boyfriend at the  time my fiance didn't think i was safe  up there so he told me to move in and  that's how i moved to the financial  district  so she had the option to leave right  anyone who doesn't know new york city  let's go through this for a second  financial district is downtown manhattan  it's where your your twin towers were  it's now where the uh freedom tower is  it's a it's a bustling area with  just a lot of people who have a lot of  money down there beautiful apartment  buildings it's safe generally now i  don't know i don't spend a lot of time  there a lot of places that used to be  safe aren't safe in new york city  anymore but at the time it was  considered safe she had the option  she was dating a guy the the post report  also talks a little bit about him  uh david segura apparently founded giant  media it says in an october 2012 report  segura predicted the company would make  eight million dollars in its third year  so apparently he's doing well great more  power to them i have an immense amount  of disrespect for people who are  successful great what i have a problem  with is that she left  the area where all the crime was  she knew that was a reality not  everybody had the opportunity to pick up  and go move in with somebody in a ritzy  area not everybody had the option that  she did at the time those people were  stuck there what about those single moms  that were stuck in that crime-ridden  area afraid to walk their kids across  the street to the store past a certain  time of night and maybe even during a  certain time of day  she left that she knows what was going  on there and she decided to then move  into the ritzy area and from that perch  in the ritzy area advocate for a defund  the police movement  that's hypocrisy i can't have that  i cannot have that and that makes up so  much of the defund the police movement  this reminds me of the people the  celebrities who walk around  they say you can't have guns ar-15s are  dangerous  we it really it's a stain on the country  and then you see a photo of them they  hop out of a car and three guys around  them  seven foot tall  with  guns to protect them  you can't have it you can't have the  police protection we need to defund the  police there's too much money you can't  have that extra police protection  you can't have that gun to protect  yourself but i can i can move to the  financial district  i'll be okay  disgusting  this stuff is disgusting  disgusting think about all those people  who suffer at the consequence of  defunding the police of having less  policemen and police women on the  streets having those departments have  less funding and can't escape  to a rich fiancee's apartment  in the financial district  i'm guessing that they wouldn't be  voting for her you know whose backs are  cynthia nixon  cynthia nixon from sex in the city who  probably can afford to have as much arm  security as she wants while she's out  there talking about how guns are bad and  you  being able to protect yourself and your  family is a bad thing  i can't with this stuff anymore  and what's always fascinating to me is  about the deep fun the police movement  they simultaneously want these people  simultaneously want to defund the police  and disarm you  do they want you to die i ask this  sincerely  you can't you don't have a gun in your  home because they don't want you to to  defend yourself okay you pick up the  phone to call the police and because the  the police movement has been defunded  money has been pulled and stripped they  have less police officers so that that  person you call is busy doing something  else they can't rush to you they get to  you a little bit later maybe there's a  10-minute delay on that from what would  have been  who suffers you do  you do maybe you don't have the luxury  of an armed guard outside your door the  way the cynthia nixons of the world can  afford